{
  "_about": "Component spec for pos-feature-card (docs/inspect refactor, component migration batch, 2026-08-26). Single source of truth for the Variants/Usage/Tokens tabs on /style-guide \"Feature card\" section. Reuses the already-curated usage prose from COMP_CONFIGS['feature-card'].usage and token data from the existing inspect-feature-card.liquid (verified-accurate, currently-live data) restructured into the new schema. Single representative variant — this component's preview shows one instance (no Variant/Base toggle needed per the 2026-08-25/26 \"multiple sub-variants side by side\" rule). Regenerate the spec partial with the script in RULES.md 6.4 if the source data changes; do not hand-edit token values here. Updated 2026-08-27: added usageExample/props/composedOf (Target architecture point 1 fields that were left empty when this spec was first generated).",
  "component": "feature-card",
  "name": "Feature card",
  "description": "Presenting a self-contained piece of content — a feature, section, or offer — with an icon, title, description, and optional action buttons.",
  "whenToUse": [
    "Presenting a self-contained piece of content — a feature, section, or offer — with an icon, title, description, and optional action buttons.",
    "Grouping related information in a visually distinct, elevated surface."
  ],
  "whenNotToUse": [
    "Navigating to another page — use a link or a button instead.",
    "Showing tabular or list data — use a table or list component."
  ],
  "do": [
    "Include an icon in <code>.pos-feature-card-icon</code> to give the card visual identity.",
    "Add <code>.pos-feature-card--centered</code> to center all content when the card stands alone or is in a symmetrical grid.",
    "<strong>Default first:</strong> always start with the built-in size variants (Small / Default / Large). Only deviate when the surrounding heading hierarchy would otherwise be broken.",
    "<strong>Page hierarchy override (cards &amp; text sections):</strong> when building a full page or UI, you may override the card's text and icon sizes to serve the document's visual and heading hierarchy — e.g. a card that acts as the main feature on a page may use a larger title size than the default. Adjust <code>.pos-feature-card-title</code>, <code>.pos-feature-card-subtitle</code>, or icon size as needed to keep headings in correct H1→H2→H3 order relative to surrounding content.",
    "Use the brand backgrounds (<code>pos-feature-card--brand-primary</code> / <code>--brand-supplementary</code>) to set a card or a group of cards apart in the brand color — they follow the brand theme and keep text, link and icon contrast. Use one background per card group, not a different color on every card."
  ],
  "dont": [
    "Nest interactive elements inside a card that is itself clickable — it creates ambiguous interaction targets.",
    "Use the card as a navigation element — it is a content container, not a link.",
    "Override the size of buttons, chips, or tags inside a card for hierarchy purposes — these components always use their own standard size variants (default or small). Typography flexibility applies to card text elements and icons only."
  ],
  "accessibility": [
    "Buttons inside <code>.pos-feature-card-actions</code> must have descriptive labels — avoid generic \"Click here\"."
  ],
  "composedOf": [
    "button",
    "link",
    "tag"
  ],
  "props": [
    {
      "name": "size",
      "type": "'pos-feature-card--small' | (none) | '--large'",
      "default": "default",
      "description": "Start with the built-in size variants; only override individual text/icon sizes to serve a specific page hierarchy — see CLAUDE.md."
    },
    {
      "name": "background",
      "type": "(none) | 'pos-feature-card--highlighted' | '--brand-primary' | '--brand-supplementary'",
      "default": "none (content background)",
      "description": "Card background. On a tinted background the icon circle turns to the content background. Brand backgrounds follow the brand theme."
    },
    {
      "name": "pos-feature-card--centered",
      "type": "boolean class",
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Centers all content — use when the card stands alone or in a symmetrical grid."
    },
    {
      "name": "badge",
      "type": "optional .pos-tag.pos-feature-card-badge",
      "default": "none",
      "description": "Optional \"New\"-style badge in the top corner."
    }
  ],
  "dimensions": {
    "state": [
      "normal",
      "hover"
    ]
  },
